## Claim
Text: "The FBI is in possession of the president of the US's son  Hunter Biden's laptop."
Claim date: October 22, 2020
Claim origin: https://nypost.com/2020/10/14/email-reveals-how-hunter-biden-introduced-ukrainian-biz-man-to-dad/

## Initial Q&A
### Was Joe Biden officially the President of the United States on October 22, 2020, or was he a presidential candidate at that time?
Answer: On October 22, 2020, Joe Biden was a presidential candidate, not the President of the United States. The search result refers to him as "the Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden" and notes that "The 2020 presidential election" had not yet occurred (it took place on November 3, 2020). At that time, Donald Trump was the sitting president, as confirmed by references to Trump's July 2019 phone call and his impeachment acquittal.

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/hunter-biden-emails-senate-homeland-security-committee-investigating-hard-drive-laptop

### Did the New York Post article published on October 14, 2020 provide specific evidence that the FBI had Hunter Biden's laptop in its possession?
Answer: No, the New York Post article itself did not provide specific evidence that the FBI had Hunter Biden's laptop in its possession. According to the search result, the Post's reporting was based on "the contents of the laptop" and documents that "Rudy Giuliani gave to the paper." The specific evidence that the FBI had subpoenaed the laptop came later from documents obtained by Fox News, which detailed a subpoena linked to a money laundering investigation in late 2019, including a "Case ID" with the classification "272D" (money laundering) and serial numbers for a laptop and hard drive.

Source URL: https://news.yahoo.com/hunter-biden-purported-laptop-connected-120252142.html

### Did the FBI officially confirm through public statements, press releases, or court documents that it had possession of a laptop belonging to Hunter Biden?
Answer: No. According to the search result, the FBI did not officially confirm possession of the laptop through public statements. The information that the FBI had the laptop came from "two senior administration officials" who spoke anonymously to Fox News, while the FBI itself "declined to confirm or deny the existence of an investigation into the laptop or the emails" and "declined to publicly comment on the situation." The FBI's only public communication referenced was a letter to Senator Ron Johnson stating it had "nothing to add at this time."

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fbi-purported-hunter-biden-laptop-sources

### Was the laptop referenced in the claim authenticated or verified through forensic means as actually belonging to Hunter Biden?
Answer: No, the laptop was not authenticated or verified through forensic means as actually belonging to Hunter Biden. According to the source, the FBI was instead "investigating the veracity of claims about the origin of the laptop and how its contents were shared with Giuliani's team," and the computer repairman who received the device, John Paul Mac Isaac, "said his poor vision prevented him from personally identifying the man as Biden."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2020/10/21/rudy-giuliani-gives-alleged-hunter-biden-laptop-authorities/6005040002/

### Through what legal process, search warrant, subpoena, or other method did the FBI allegedly obtain Hunter Biden's laptop?
Answer: According to the search result, the FBI obtained Hunter Biden's laptop and hard drive through a **subpoena** issued in connection with a money-laundering investigation. The article states: "The FBI subpoena of Hunter Biden's computer and hard drive came in connection with a money-laundering investigation, according to documents obtained by Fox News." The subpoena was signed by FBI Special Agent Joshua Wilson and executed in the FBI's Baltimore office, which covers Wilmington, Delaware.

Source URL: https://nypost.com/2020/10/21/hunter-biden-laptop-linked-to-fbi-money-laundering-probe-report/

### Did any credible source such as a court filing, congressional testimony, or law enforcement official verify that the FBI possessed Hunter Biden's laptop between October 14 and October 22, 2020?
Answer: Yes. According to the Fox News report, "multiple federal law enforcement officials, as well as two separate government officials, confirmed the authenticity" of FBI documents—including a subpoena and a "Receipt for Property" form—showing the FBI had taken possession of a laptop and hard drive purportedly belonging to Hunter Biden. Additionally, Director of National Intelligence John Ratcliffe publicly stated that week that the laptop and emails "is not part of some Russian disinformation campaign," and the underlying court subpoena issued to the repair shop owner John Paul Mac Isaac constituted a verifiable court filing, though the FBI itself declined to confirm or deny the investigation as a matter of policy.

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/laptop-hunter-biden-linked-fbi-money-laundering-probe

### What was the stated purpose of the FBI in possessing Hunter Biden's laptop, and was it connected to any active investigation?
Answer: According to the search result, the FBI took custody of Hunter Biden's laptop and an external hard drive as early as December 2019, and "is investigating the laptop materials from Joe Biden's son as part of a possible foreign disinformation operation." Specifically, "the bureau, according to the congressional source, is looking into the provenance of the material" and seeking to determine "whether the laptop dump is part of what the intelligence community's counterintelligence chief has already described as a Russian disinformation effort targeting the 2020 election." The FBI itself declined to comment, "in keeping with our standard practice of neither confirming nor denying the existence of our investigations," confirming that this was indeed an active investigation rather than mere custodial possession.

Source URL: https://www.thedailybeast.com/fbi-examining-hunter-bidens-laptop-as-foreign-op-contradicting-john-ratcliffe-trumps-intel-czar

### Did the FBI conduct a forensic examination of the laptop's contents, and if so, what was the result of that examination?
Answer: The search result does not contain information about whether the FBI conducted a forensic examination of the laptop's contents or the results of any such examination. The article focuses on the FBI's subpoena of the laptop in connection with a money laundering investigation and the FBI's possession of the device, but it does not address a forensic analysis or its findings.

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/laptop-hunter-biden-linked-fbi-money-laundering-probe

### Is there any public record, news report, or official document that contradicts the claim that the FBI possessed Hunter Biden's laptop as of October 22, 2020?
Answer: The search result does not contradict the claim; rather, it **supports** it. The Fox News article explicitly states, "The FBI is in possession of the laptop purportedly belonging to Hunter Biden," citing two senior administration officials, and also references FBI paperwork that details serial numbers for a laptop and hard drive "taken into possession." While the FBI itself declined to confirm or deny (standard practice), no source in this article disputes that the bureau had the laptop.

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fbi-purported-hunter-biden-laptop-sources

### Did the FBI make any public statements regarding Hunter Biden's laptop between October 14, 2020 and October 22, 2020 that either confirmed or denied possession of the device?
Answer: Based on the search result, the FBI did not make any public statements between October 14 and October 22, 2020 that either confirmed or denied possession of Hunter Biden's laptop. Instead, when contacted by congressional committee staff and later by Senator Johnson on October 17, 2020, the FBI "responded that it would not confirm or deny any information," and "still has not provided satisfactory answers." The only public indication of FBI possession during that window came from anonymous officials cited in a Fox News report dated October 21, 2020, not from an official FBI statement.

